BMP/TIFF integration

libnsbmp 0.1.7: MIT. Full copyright and permission text: libnsbmp-LICENSE.
libtiff 4.7.2: TIFF license. Full text: libtiff-LICENSE; additional original
linked-source copyright headers: RASTER-RUNTIME-NOTICE.
The tif_hash_set helper by Even Rouault retains its MIT permission text in
RASTER-RUNTIME-NOTICE.
zlib 1.3.2: Zlib license. Full text: zlib-LICENSE.

The libraries are built from the pinned unmodified source subsets in
sources/raster/upstream. Original download URLs and SHA-256 checksums are
recorded in sources/raster/sources.lock.json. The source selection excludes
tests, sample images and command-line tools; it does not alter the libraries.
The application adapters and build script are Copyright (c) 2026 Ilya Barilo,
MIT; see sources/raster/PROJECT-LICENSE.
The build script corrects three libnsbmp header-length checks for ICO DIBs,
which do not contain a BMP file header. The original source archive remains
unchanged. The MIT adapter expands sub-byte channel values to full-range RGBA8.

Generated JavaScript and WebAssembly use Emscripten 6.0.9 / emmalloc and the
C runtime. Preserve Emscripten-LICENSE, Emscripten-AUTHORS, musl-COPYRIGHT,
compiler-rt-LICENSE, compiler-rt-CREDITS, llvm-libc-LICENSE and the exact
linked-source headers collected in RASTER-RUNTIME-NOTICE.

JPEG-in-TIFF compatibility uses UTIF and libjpeg-turbo. Their notices remain
in UTIF-JPEG-NOTICE, JPEG-NOTICE and JPEG-RUNTIME-NOTICE.
